      <h1>Best Time to Visit Zanzibar 2025: Month-by-Month Guide</h1>
      <p class="blog-excerpt">When is the best time to visit Zanzibar in 2025? Month-by-month weather breakdown, activity recommendations, crowd levels, and pricing for every travel style.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="blog-content">
      <section>
        <h2>Quick Answer: Best Time for You</h2>
        <table class="rate-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Travel Style</th><th>Best Months</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Perfect weather, all activities</td><td>Jun–Oct</td><td>Dry, cool, low humidity, calm seas</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Budget / fewer crowds</td><td>Mar–May, Nov</td><td>Green season discounts, lush scenery</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Kite surfing</td><td>Jun–Sep</td><td>Consistent 15–25 knot cross-onshore winds</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Diving / Snorkeling</td><td>Jan–Mar, Jun–Oct</td><td>Best visibility (20–30m), calm seas</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Families with kids</td><td>Jun–Oct, Dec–Feb</td><td>Calm seas, minimal rain, kid-friendly</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Honeymoon / Romance</td><td>Jun–Oct, Jan–Feb</td><td>Sunsets, private beaches, luxury deals</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Safari combos</td><td>Jun–Oct, Jan–Feb</td><td>Dry season = best wildlife viewing</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Festivals / Culture</td><td>Feb (Sauti za Busara), Jul (Mwaka Kogwa)</td><td>Major cultural events</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Month-by-Month Breakdown</h2>
        
        <h3>January ☀️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Hot, dry, 28–32°C, low humidity</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 28°C, calm, excellent visibility</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> High (post-holiday)</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Beach, diving, safari combos, honeymoons</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Peak season rates</li></ul>
        
        <h3>February 🎭</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Hot, dry, 28–32°C</li><li><strong>Event:</strong> <strong>Sauti za Busara</strong> (African music festival, Stone Town)</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 29°C, calm</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Culture + beach, festival-goers</li><li><strong>Book early:</strong> Festival week books out months ahead</li></ul>
        
        <h3>March 🌧️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Hot, humid, long rains begin late March</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 29°C, variable visibility</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> Low</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Budget travelers, green scenery, fewer tourists</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> 30–50% off peak rates</li></ul>
        
        <h3>April 🌧️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Peak long rains, daily downpours, 26–30°C</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> Rougher, reduced visibility</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> Very low</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Maximum discounts, lush green landscapes, spa/wellness</li><li><strong>Note:</strong> Some marine activities cancelled on rough days</li></ul>
        
        <h3>May 🌧️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Rains tapering, humid, 26–30°C</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> Improving</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Late deals, fewer tourists, green landscapes</li><li><strong>Transition:</strong> Rains usually end late May</li></ul>
        
        <h3>June ☀️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Dry season starts, 24–28°C, low humidity</li><li><strong>Wind:</strong> Kite season begins (15–20 knots)</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 26–27°C, calm</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Kite surfing start, diving, perfect weather</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Shoulder to peak transition</li></ul>
        
        <h3>July ☀️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Cool, dry, 23–27°C, very low humidity</li><li><strong>Event:</strong> <strong>Mwaka Kogwa</strong> (Shirazi New Year, Makunduchi, late July)</li><li><strong>Wind:</strong> Peak kite season (20–25 knots)</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Kite surfing, culture, families, safari combos</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Peak season</li></ul>
        
        <h3>August ☀️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Cool, dry, 23–27°C</li><li><strong>Wind:</strong> Consistent kite winds</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> High (European summer holidays)</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Kite surfing, families, diving, safari</li><li><strong>Book early:</strong> Peak demand</li></ul>
        
        <h3>September ☀️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Dry, warming, 24–29°C</li><li><strong>Wind:</strong> Kite season ending</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 26°C, excellent visibility</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Diving, snorkeling, quieter than Jul/Aug</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Peak to shoulder transition</li></ul>
        
        <h3>October ☀️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Dry, warm, 25–30°C</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 27°C, calm, best visibility</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> Moderate</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Diving, snorkeling, honeymoons, value</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Shoulder season deals start</li></ul>
        
        <h3>November 🌤️</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Short rains begin, 27–31°C, brief showers</li><li><strong>Sea:</strong> 28°C, generally calm</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> Low</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Shoulder deals, fewer tourists, good weather windows</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> 20–30% off peak</li></ul>
        
        <h3>December 🎄</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Weather:</strong> Hot, humid, short rains ending, 28–32°C</li><li><strong>Event:</strong> Christmas/New Year festivities</li><li><strong>Crowds:</strong> High (festive season)</li><li><strong>Best for:</strong> Festive beach holiday, diving, culture</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Peak (festive surcharges apply Dec 20–Jan 7)</li></ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Activity-Specific Best Times</h2>
        <table class="rate-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Best Months</th><th>Avoid</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Kite Surfing</td><td>Jun–Sep</td><td>Nov–Apr (inconsistent wind)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Scuba Diving</td><td>Jan–Mar, Jun–Oct</td><td>Apr–May (rough seas, low viz)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Snorkeling</td><td>Jan–Mar, Jun–Oct</td><td>Apr–May</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Dolphin Tour</td><td>Jun–Oct (calm seas)</td><td>Apr–May (rough)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Safari (Mainland)</td><td>Jun–Oct, Jan–Feb</td><td>Mar–May (dispersed wildlife)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Whale Sharks (Mafia)</td><td>Oct–Mar</td><td>Apr–Sep</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Humpback Whales</td><td>Jul–Sep</td><td>Oct–Jun</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Turtle Hatching</td><td>Feb–May (Nungwi)</td><td>Jun–Jan</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bioluminescence</td><td>Jul–Sep (new moon)</td><td>Full moon periods</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Regional Micro-Climates</h2>
        <p>Zanzibar's weather varies by coast:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>North (Nungwi/Kendwa):</strong> Least tidal variation, all-day swimming, windiest</li>
          <li><strong>East (Matemwe/Paje/Jambiani):</strong> Strong tidal variation, best kite spots</li>
          <li><strong>South (Michamvi/Kizimkazi):</strong> Calmer, protected bays, dolphin tours</li>
          <li><strong>West (Stone Town/Fumba):</strong> Most sheltered, mangrove channels</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <div class="card" style="padding:1.5rem;margin-top:2rem;background:#f0f9ff;border-left:4px solid #00667c;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">💡 Our Recommendation</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;">For first-time visitors wanting the classic Zanzibar experience: <strong>June–October</strong> offers the most reliable weather, calm seas for all water activities, and the full range of tours. For budget-conscious travelers who don't mind occasional rain: <strong>March–May or November</strong> offer incredible value and lush landscapes.</p>
